%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5a0f9465ab7696142ac3a15a37af66c2, type: 3}
  m_Name: Richard
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterId: char_richard
  displayName: Richard
  profilePicture: {fileID: 0}
  contactButton: {fileID: 0}
  scheduledMessages:
  - messageId: richard_introduction
    triggerHour: 20
    triggerMinute: 51
    requiredClues: []
    grantedClues: []
    messages:
    - sender: 1
      text: 'Good Evening, my wife, Evelyn told me to contact you regarding her ''case''.
        Personally I see no need for it, however I will tell you anything you need
        to know.


        Richard'
      delay: 0.25
  - messageId: richard_on_bryans_textile_knowledge
    triggerHour: 21
    triggerMinute: 20
    requiredClues: []
    grantedClues:
    - bryans_textile_knowledge
    messages:
    - sender: 1
      text: It feels a little silly to mention this, but Evelyn told me to describe
        anything I witness.
      delay: 0
    - sender: 1
      text: I was just talking to Bryan... how does he suddenly so much about the
        textiles industry? He's never been interested in conversation about it before,
        he normally tells me to 'just retire' if I bring up work.
      delay: 2.3
  - messageId: richard_on_missing_pocket_watch
    triggerHour: 22
    triggerMinute: 10
    requiredClues: []
    grantedClues:
    - missing_pocket_watch
    messages:
    - sender: 1
      text: Something terrible has happened! my grandfathers pocket watch has disappeared!
      delay: 0
    - sender: 1
      text: I was on my way to the restroom when I noticed it was not in it's display
        case on the hallway cabinet, I am going to look around the house for it,
        it cannot have gone far.
      delay: 1.9
  - messageId: richard_forgives_alex
    triggerHour: 23
    triggerMinute: 15
    requiredClues:
    - alexs_admission
    - bryan_says_alex_lies
    grantedClues:
    - bryan_is_wrong
    messages:
    - sender: 1
      text: Alex has just told me that he is the one whole stole the watch and I
        have now returned it to its rightful position, I am furious.
      delay: 0
    - sender: 1
      text: But I have ultimately chose to forgive him, he wanted to buy a ring so
        he could propose to his partner, and he genuinely felt bad.
      delay: 3.25
    - sender: 1
      text: He's going to be pulling double shifts for the next six weeks but, he's
        a good lad at heart.
      delay: 2
  questions:
  - questionId: Q01R
    questionText: What do you know about 'Count Backward'?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - backstory
    grantedClues:
    - the_diary
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: My wife had found a diary of some description, and is up in arms at the
        thought of a spirit. I thought to myself a spirit? seriously? It is all a
        laughable farce to me my friend.
      delay: 2.1
  - questionId: Q03R
    questionText: Evelyn told me to ask you about Alex, it seems to me he could be
      withdrawing information?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - richard_trusts_alex
    - the_diary
    grantedClues:
    - 
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: No, not Alex, he's a good lad, but a little... shy, you could say. Especially
        around new people. He's a great worker with me at the mill.
      delay: 1.8
  - questionId: Q04R
    questionText: How long have you known Bryan?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - richard_bryan_relationship
    grantedClues:
    - richards_faulty_memory_1
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: For a long time, we were teenagers when we met, I believe?
      delay: 1.1
    - sender: 1
      text: Sorry, my memory isn't perfect.
      delay: 0.8
  - questionId: Q05R
    questionText: Bryan said you have known each other since primary school, and
      that he worked in the mill with you in his 20's?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - bryans_textile_knowledge
    - richards_faulty_memory_2
    - richard_bryan_relationship
    - richards_faulty_memory_1
    grantedClues:
    - bryans_faulty_memory
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: No, he's got that wrong, we attended the same secondary school togethor,
        he was living abroad for the majority of his childhood, maybe his misremembered.
      delay: 1.86
    - sender: 1
      text: As for the mill- he worked with me and my father for maybe two weeks
        when we were in our early 20's, we ended up falling out over it, and he hasn't
        liked speaking about the industry since... until today.
      delay: 3.8
  - questionId: Q08R
    questionText: Did you see anybody leave the drawing room recently?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - missing_pocket_watch
    grantedClues: []
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: "No, I did not, maybe ask the others, I need to keep looking!\t"
      delay: 2.85
  - questionId: Q12R
    questionText: People have noticed you wandering around the house, staring at
      clocks, are you okay?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - what_is_richard_doing
    grantedClues: []
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: I'm concerned for my posessions! if one has gone missing, I certainly
        don't want to be losing more!
      delay: 2.25
